    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35917" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνοικ-ίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>settle in</i> a place, <i>plant, fix in,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				252
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρά τισί τι ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Epin.</u>
					978c
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλοεθνεῖς -ισάμενοι γυναῖκας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					11.5.4
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>take up one's abode in</i> a place, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.68
			</span></i> (so in aor.
			
				Med.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.2
			</span></i>); also, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνοικέω</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				1.3
			</span></i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιτηδεύμασι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ax.</u>
					371c
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>introduce</i> a tenant into premises, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. καὶ ἐξοικίζειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>BGU</u>
					1116.18
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(i B. C.)</span>.</div>
